{
  "_comment": [
    "OUT_OF_SCOPE training negatives -- an 8th, internal-only class.",
    "This is a SEPARATE file on purpose: data/raw/intents.json keeps exactly 7 intents so the",
    "public API contract and the 'every intent has a handler' test stay valid. At inference",
    "'out_of_scope' is mapped to the public 'fallback' intent (see app/nlp/intent_classifier.py).",
    "Authored independently of data/eval/ood_eval.json; the two must share no normalized text.",
    "tests/test_ood.py enforces that, plus dedupe-after-normalize and per-language minimums.",
    "NEAR-MISS REVIEW: items that look like a real intent but are NOT are deliberately included",
    "(e.g. 'cancel my gym membership', 'track my flight') because rejecting shop-adjacent",
    "non-shop requests is exactly the behaviour we want. Genuine in-domain phrasings are NOT here.",
    "Verified: 0 normalized overlap with data/raw/intents.json and data/eval/ood_eval.json, 0 internal duplicates.",
    "Downsampled per language to hit ~33% of the corpus. The 25-30% ask in the brief cannot be met while keeping the per-language minimums (100+100+100+40=340 negatives already forces 340/1048=32.4%).",
    "Language-neutral strings (emoji, Latin gibberish, foreign greetings) are kept once, in the first language bucket they appeared in, so no normalized text is duplicated across languages."
  ],
